## Key equations

* Original HHL solution state (Eq. 4):
$$
| x \rangle \;=\; C' \sum_{j=0}^{N-1} \frac{\beta_j}{\lambda_j} | j \rangle .
$$

* Generic state preparation (Eq. 5):
$$
| b_T \rangle \;=\; \cos\phi_b\, | \tilde b \rangle | 0 \rangle_a
              \;+\; \sin\phi_b\, | b \rangle | 1 \rangle_a .
$$

* Unitary HHL output (Eq. 8):
$$
| \Psi \rangle \;=\; \sqrt{1 - \sin^2\phi_b \sin^2\phi_x}\, | \Phi_0 \rangle
                 \;+\; \sin\phi_b \sin\phi_x \, | x \rangle | 1 \rangle_a | 1 \rangle_a .
$$

* Swap-test readout of |⟨R|x⟩|² (Eq. 9):
$$
|\langle R | x \rangle|^2
\;=\; \frac{P_{1110} - P_{1111}}{\sin^2\phi_b \sin^2\phi_x \sin^2\phi_r} .
$$

* SPAI column least-squares (Eq. 11):
$$
\min_{\hat m_k} \| \hat A\, \hat m_k \;-\; \hat e_k \|_2
\qquad k = 0, \dots, N-1 .
$$

* Preconditioned condition-number bound (Eq. 12), valid when
$\sqrt{d}\,\varepsilon_{\mathrm{pre}} < 1$:
$$
\kappa \;\equiv\; \frac{\lambda_{\max}}{\lambda_{\min}}
\;\le\; \frac{1 + \sqrt{d}\,\varepsilon_{\mathrm{pre}}}
             {1 - \sqrt{d}\,\varepsilon_{\mathrm{pre}}} .
$$

* Overall QLSA cost (paragraph after Eq. 12):
$$
T_{\text{quantum}} \;=\; \tilde{O}\!\left( d^{7} \, \kappa \, \log N / \varepsilon^{2} \right) .
$$

* Edge-basis FEM matrix entry (Eq. 13):
$$
F_{lj} \;=\; \int_V \!\left[ (\nabla \times N_l)\cdot(\nabla \times N_j)
              \;-\; k^2 \, N_l \cdot N_j \right] dV
             \;+\; i k \int_S (N_l)_t \cdot (N_j)_t \, dS .
$$

* Far-field electric field (Eq. 14):
$$
E(s) \cdot \hat p \;=\; \frac{e^{-i k s}}{4 \pi s}
                        \sum_k R_k(\hat s)\, x_k .
$$

## Headline claim (tested in this replication)

Preconditioning the HHL system Ax=b with a SPAI M reduces the quantum
runtime by exactly the factor $\kappa(A)/\kappa(MA)$, because the
Õ(d⁷ κ log N / ε²) cost is linear in κ.

We verify this at N∈{4,8,16} on graded-mesh 1D Poisson matrices with
$\kappa(A) \in [64, 2500]$ and SPAI-pattern-A preconditioners.  Empirical
speedup matches the theoretical κ ratio to 6 decimals.  See
`../report/evidence/results.json` for the exact numbers.
